# [[ project_name ]]

[[ description ]]

dbt project generated by **fast-stack-forge ⚡**. Adapter: `[[ adapter ]]`. Architecture: `[[ archi ]]`.

## Getting started

[% if standalone %]
```bash
cp .env.example .env   # fill in your credentials
make install           # uv sync + dbt deps
make debug             # check the connection
make build             # seeds, models, snapshots and tests
```

Run `make help` to list every command.
[% else %]
[% if profiles_dir %]
Local connection settings live in `[[ profiles_dir ]]/profiles.yml` (variables from `.env`):

```bash
export DBT_PROFILES_DIR=[[ profiles_dir ]]
[% else %]
```bash
[% endif %]
uv run dbt deps
uv run dbt build
```
[% endif %]

## Layers

| Folder | Role | Materialization |
|---|---|---|
| `models/[[ arch.layers[0] ]]` | Clean, rename and cast the raw data (one model per source table) | view |
| `models/[[ arch.layers[1] ]]` | [[ arch.roles[1] ]] | [[ 'view' if archi == 'default' else 'table' ]] |
| `models/[[ arch.layers[2] ]]` | [[ arch.roles[2] ]] | table |
[% if examples %]

## Example data

The models read the CSV files in `seeds/` so the project builds right away.
To use your real data, declare your tables in `models/[[ arch.layers[0] ]]/_sources.yml`
and replace `ref('raw_…')` with `source('raw', '<table>')` in the `[[ arch.layers[0] ]]` models.
[% endif %]

## Add a model

```bash
fast-stack-forge make:dbt fct_sales --layer [[ arch.layers[2] ]]            # SQL table
fast-stack-forge make:dbt fct_events --layer [[ arch.layers[2] ]] --incremental
```
